Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.15,0:00:16.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Yu-Gi-Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.27,0:00:17.62,Default,,0,0,0,,For you, King of Kings!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.27,0:01:19.31,Default,,0,0,0,,constant state of fear and\Neventually destroy you.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.33,0:01:21.95,Default,,0,0,0,,It is you who should be afraid.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.03,0:01:27.57,Default,,0,0,0,,You have no monsters left and you're down\Nto your last 150 life points. That's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.87,0:01:28.70,Default,,0,0,0,,However,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.78,0:01:31.99,Default,,0,0,0,,the evil ghost of Dark\NSanctuary is now protecting me,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.09,0:01:34.56,Default,,0,0,0,,which will change my fortune dramatically.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.29,0:01:37.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Your ghosts don't frighten me.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.53,0:01:40.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Without a single monster\Nto defend your life points,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.45,0:01:45.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I will win this duel and remove you from\Nthe Battle City finals in one attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.45,0:01:47.51,Default,,0,0,0,,You're more foolish than I thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.61,0:01:51.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Dark Sanctuary provides me\Npower beyond your understanding.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.11,0:01:54.40,Default,,0,0,0,,But if you're so confident,\Nthen go ahead and attack me.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.77,0:01:58.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Gamma, the Magnet Warrior,\Nattack his life points directly!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.61,0:02:01.44,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.65,0:02:03.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Evil ghost counterattack!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.49,0:02:06.67,Default,,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.77,0:02:10.24,Default,,0,0,0,,My monster's attack didn't work\Nand I was attacked instead!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.09,0:02:12.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Very observant, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.83,0:02:16.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Your monster is possessed by the\Nevil ghost of my Dark Sanctuary.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.97,0:02:18.05,Default,,0,0,0,,It's possessed?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.27,0:02:22.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, and that is how I was able to\Nturn your own monster against you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.41,0:02:25.59,Default,,0,0,0,,And have you possessed all of them?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.89,0:02:27.99,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll just have to figure\Nthat out for yourself
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.07,0:02:30.95,Default,,0,0,0,,if you have the nerve to\Ntry and attack me again.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.25,0:02:34.66,Default,,0,0,0,,And of course, possession is\Nonly one of my card's powers.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.09,0:02:39.39,Default,,0,0,0,,But you'll find out what else Dark\NSanctuary is capable of soon enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.55,0:02:41.85,Default,,0,0,0,,in the meantime we shall\Ndeal with the situation
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.93,0:02:46.03,Default,,0,0,0,,at hand go on i will since\Nyou made the mistake of
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.11,0:02:49.15,Default,,0,0,0,,attacking me with a monster\Nthat was possessed half
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.23,0:02:51.39,Default,,0,0,0,,of your monster's attack\Npoints come out of your
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.47,0:02:56.03,Default,,0,0,0,,life points and then just\Nto make sure they don't
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.11,0:02:58.81,Default,,0,0,0,,go to waste the life points\Nyou lost will simply be
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.89,0:03:03.81,Default,,0,0,0,,added to mine your life\Npoints are still minimal
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.89,0:03:06.79,Default,,0,0,0,,they'll be gone soon we'll\Njust Let's see about that,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.87,0:03:07.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.78,0:03:10.69,Default,,0,0,0,,You have no idea the terror\Nthat lurks in my deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.05,0:03:13.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's see what's next. Are you ready?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.37,0:03:17.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I play Destiny Board.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.45,0:03:20.47,Default,,0,0,0,,You're finished. Destiny\NBoard? What does it do?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.61,0:03:22.15,Default,,0,0,0,,You're about to find out.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.77,0:03:24.63,Default,,0,0,0,,That's weird.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.81,0:03:26.51,Default,,0,0,0,,All that fuss for a board game?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.59,0:03:29.77,Default,,0,0,0,,I saw one of those things\Nonce at a haunted fun house.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.13,0:03:31.99,Default,,0,0,0,,You mean there's gonna be more ghosts?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.07,0:03:32.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on, Jelly.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.07,0:03:34.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Isn't this all just a game?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.37,0:03:37.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, guys, let's hope so.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.53,0:03:38.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll ask you again.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.13,0:03:40.51,Default,,0,0,0,,What does this card do?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.21,0:03:42.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Answer me!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.53,0:03:44.87,Default,,0,0,0,,It's quite simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.15,0:03:47.29,Default,,0,0,0,,My destiny board gives me the ability to
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.37,0:03:50.01,Default,,0,0,0,,communicate with lost\Nsouls of the Shadow Realm.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.09,0:03:54.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Using the letters on this board, they\Nshall spell out a message for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.51,0:03:58.75,Default,,0,0,0,,So, Yogi, it's time for you to receive\Nthe first letter of your message.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.99,0:04:01.29,Default,,0,0,0,,And that letter is F.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.79,0:04:09.19,Default,,0,0,0,,What is the destiny board going\Nto spell out? You'll see each.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.27,0:04:13.33,Default,,0,0,0,,turn the destiny board will\Nreveal one letter and then after
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.41,0:04:16.95,Default,,0,0,0,,five turns pass and all five\Nletters are revealed this duel
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.03,0:04:18.11,Default,,0,0,0,,will end and you'll lose
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.19,0:04:24.97,Default,,0,0,0,,absolutely everything you get your
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.05,0:04:28.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Destiny Board doesn't frighten\Nme. I'll defeat you well before
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.89,0:04:32.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Its message is spelled out in\Nfour more turns after all. It's
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.77,0:04:37.07,Default,,0,0,0,,my destiny to win come on yugi\Nshow this creepazoid who's boss
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.15,0:04:41.97,Default,,0,0,0,,this looks bad yes and if yugi\Nhas any hopes of winning this
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.05,0:04:45.23,Default,,0,0,0,,duel before that destiny board\Ncounts down to his destruction
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.31,0:04:49.51,Default,,0,0,0,,he had better summon that\Negyptian god card of his before
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.59,0:04:56.47,Default,,0,0,0,,long the pharaoh will be finished\Nfor good yugi with my evil
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.55,0:04:59.99,Default,,0,0,0,,ghost possessing your monsters\Nand my destiny board on the
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.07,0:05:03.95,Default,,0,0,0,,playing field you're done only\Nfour more turns and victory
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.03,0:05:09.75,Default,,0,0,0,,is mine now i play the dark\Ndoor with this magic card on the
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.83,0:05:15.53,Default,,0,0,0,,field you can only attack once\Nper turn your chances of defeating
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.61,0:05:19.53,Default,,0,0,0,,me have just decreased and next\Ni'll play earthbound spirit
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.51,0:05:23.69,Default,,0,0,0,,But it won't be around for long.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.95,0:05:27.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I plan to sacrifice it. You see,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.03,0:05:30.63,Default,,0,0,0,,in order to keep my Dark\NSanctuary card in play,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.71,0:05:33.06,Default,,0,0,0,,I need to sacrifice a monster each turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.25,0:05:34.25,Default,,0,0,0,,So be gone!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.11,0:05:39.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Time for me to put an end to this.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.13,0:05:44.79,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, since he has Dark Door in\Nplay, I can only make one attack per turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.93,0:05:47.09,Default,,0,0,0,,So I have to make this attack count.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.35,0:05:51.09,Default,,0,0,0,,But I can't use my Magnet Warrior\Nsince it's possessed by an evil ghost,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.17,0:05:53.01,Default,,0,0,0,,thanks to his Dark Sanctuary card.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.09,0:05:55.67,Default,,0,0,0,,If I attack with it, I'll\Nlose life points again.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.75,0:05:59.17,Default,,0,0,0,,So, my best bet is to attack\Nhim with my Dark Magician Girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.25,0:06:02.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Since he has no monsters protecting\Nhim and only 900 life points,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.87,0:06:05.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I can wipe him out with one direct attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.35,0:06:08.23,Default,,0,0,0,,As long as he doesn't stop my\Nattack with that face down card,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.31,0:06:09.66,Default,,0,0,0,,this duel will be over.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.63,0:06:11.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Well then...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.57,0:06:15.57,Default,,0,0,0,,You seem to have trouble\Nmaking up your mind, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.69,0:06:17.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps you should surrender now.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.69,0:06:19.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Never!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.60,0:06:21.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I summon Karibo in defense mode!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.69,0:06:26.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, my dark magician girl,\Nattack his life points directly!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.63,0:06:30.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Dark ghost counterattack!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.45,0:06:35.61,Default,,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.85,0:06:37.21,Default,,0,0,0,,She was possessed.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.71,0:06:41.45,Default,,0,0,0,,With each turn, I can choose a different\Nmonster for my spirit to possess.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.53,0:06:44.43,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, you lose even\Nmore of your life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.55,0:06:46.83,Default,,0,0,0,,But fortunately, they get added to my own.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.91,0:06:49.47,Default,,0,0,0,,My Dark Sanctuary is full of surprises.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.83,0:06:53.42,Default,,0,0,0,,And since your turn is over,\Nyou know what's about to happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.85,0:06:55.23,Default,,0,0,0,,What? Tell me!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.49,0:06:57.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Destiny Board gets another letter.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.11,0:07:02.49,Default,,0,0,0,,And the second letter is I.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.91,0:07:04.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Only three letters left.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.59,0:07:06.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, guys, look.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.97,0:07:09.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Now it's spelled F-I. Wait! Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.71,0:07:12.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Our dual disks only have five slots,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.19,0:07:15.69,Default,,0,0,0,,which means only five magic\Ncards can be in play at once,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.77,0:07:18.27,Default,,0,0,0,,and each of your letters\Nis one magic card.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.35,0:07:23.23,Default,,0,0,0,,So as long as your Dark Door card is in\Nplay, you can't spell out your entire word.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.31,0:07:25.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Very observant, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.33,0:07:30.45,Default,,0,0,0,,However, with Dark Sanctuary, I can\Nplay more than five magic cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.93,0:07:32.23,Default,,0,0,0,,In other words,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.57,0:07:35.81,Default,,0,0,0,,even with my Dark Door magic\Ncard on the playing field,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.89,0:07:40.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I can still play all five letters of\Nthe Destiny Board and finish you off.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.47,0:07:46.23,Default,,0,0,0,,You mean your Dark Sanctuary\Ncard allows you to play extra
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.31,0:07:49.55,Default,,0,0,0,,magic cards and possess my\Nmonsters with an evil ghost?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.95,0:07:52.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, and that is what\Nmakes me unstoppable.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.07,0:07:55.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi, your hope of winning is over.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.23,0:07:59.07,Default,,0,0,0,,In just three short turns,\Nyou will be finished.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.31,0:08:02.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Say goodbye to the finals. Oh, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.23,0:08:04.83,Default,,0,0,0,,He better think of something quick.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.91,0:08:06.59,Default,,0,0,0,,If Yugi could just figure out which one of
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.67,0:08:08.79,Default,,0,0,0,,his monsters is possessed\Nby Dark Sanctuary,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.87,0:08:10.59,Default,,0,0,0,,then he could launch an attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.67,0:08:12.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I still think he has a\Nchance to win this duel,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.05,0:08:14.97,Default,,0,0,0,,but he can't keep losing life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.05,0:08:18.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe he's overthinking all this\Nand the key is not to think at all,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.89,0:08:19.95,Default,,0,0,0,,like Tristan does.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.99,0:08:23.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Joey, Yugi's gonna win, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.79,0:08:26.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, Yugi'll pull through,\Nbut it sure won't be easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.95,0:08:31.11,Default,,0,0,0,,As long as the magic of Dark Sanctuary\Nsurrounds us, I'm in control.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.53,0:08:35.93,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'll need to sacrifice this\Nmonster in order to keep it that way.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.65,0:08:38.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I summon Sangin!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.95,0:08:45.57,Default,,0,0,0,,And now I'll sacrifice it to\Nmaintain the power of Dark Sanctuary.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.95,0:08:50.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Sangin's special effect\Nallows me to draw one
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.49,0:08:53.26,Default,,0,0,0,,more card after it's been\Nsent to the graveyard
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.71,0:08:54.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Now,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.63,0:08:59.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's see what you can do. Not\Nmuch, I'm sure. You're wrong,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.49,0:09:02.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I draw. It's time to\Npossess Yugi's next monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.17,0:09:06.99,Default,,0,0,0,,But which one should my ghost hide within?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.15,0:09:12.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, he'd never suspect that I'd choose\NDark Magician Girl twice in a row.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.23,0:09:14.81,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the perfect plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.19,0:09:19.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I know one of my three monsters is\Npossessed by the Ghost of Dark Sanctuary.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.41,0:09:20.55,Default,,0,0,0,,But which one?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.75,0:09:22.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I doubt it's Karibu.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.57,0:09:24.85,Default,,0,0,0,,He's too weak for me\Nto attack with anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.93,0:09:27.19,Default,,0,0,0,,So that leaves me with two choices.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.67,0:09:31.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Gamma the Magnet Warrior\Nor the Dark Magician Girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.29,0:09:32.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Which is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.43,0:09:35.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I can only attack once\Nthanks to his Dark Door card.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.09,0:09:37.45,Default,,0,0,0,,And if I choose the wrong\Nmonster to attack with,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.53,0:09:40.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll lose more life points,\Nand he'll gain them.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.53,0:09:42.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't mess up, or I'm finished.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.65,0:09:47.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Proceed with your attack, Yugi,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.59,0:09:48.73,Default,,0,0,0,,but choose wisely,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.97,0:09:53.32,Default,,0,0,0,,for one of your monsters is possessed\Nby the evil ghost of Dark Sanctuary.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.49,0:09:55.57,Default,,0,0,0,,I know this monster isn't possessed,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.65,0:09:58.71,Default,,0,0,0,,because I just drew it, but\Nhis attack points are low,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.79,0:10:01.65,Default,,0,0,0,,so I'll just use it to\Nprotect my life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.83,0:10:03.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I summon Big Shield Gardener!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.07,0:10:05.69,Default,,0,0,0,,In defense mode!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.57,0:10:08.85,Default,,0,0,0,,That was pointless.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.31,0:10:13.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing can protect your life points\Nfrom the ghost of Dark Sanctuary.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.93,0:10:16.13,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, time to attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.33,0:10:19.33,Default,,0,0,0,,But I gotta make sure I don't\Nchoose the monster that's possessed,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.41,0:10:23.13,Default,,0,0,0,,or half of that monster's attack points\Nwill be taken out of my life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.21,0:10:26.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Since my Magnet Warrior has less\Nattack points, I'll choose him.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.53,0:10:28.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Gamma the Magnet Warrior, attack now!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.69,0:10:33.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi didn't choose the possessed\Nmonster, but no matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.07,0:10:36.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I have a card to change all that.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.61,0:10:40.11,Default,,0,0,0,,You've triggered my trap card,\NDark Spirit of the Silent.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.39,0:10:46.43,Default,,0,0,0,,This card instantly stops your\NMagnet Warrior from attacking me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.69,0:10:51.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you honestly believe I'd let you\Nattack my life points directly, Yugi?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.23,0:10:52.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Never, and there's more.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.23,0:10:58.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Once my trap card stops your warrior, it\Nwill force Dark Magician Girl to attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.31,0:10:59.14,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.22,0:11:03.02,Default,,0,0,0,,If my Dark Magician Girl is the monster\Nthat's possessed and she attacks you,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.11,0:11:06.31,Default,,0,0,0,,then that means I'll lose\Nmore life points. Correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.61,0:11:10.95,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'm afraid she is, so say\Ngoodbye to 1,250 life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.39,0:11:18.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like you get weaker as my\Nlife points grow higher and higher.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.01,0:11:21.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi's running out of\Nlife points pretty fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.67,0:11:22.63,Default,,0,0,0,,He's a goner.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.19,0:11:24.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.13,0:11:26.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you saying Yugi's gonna lose?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.67,0:11:27.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.73,0:11:30.99,Default,,0,0,0,,When one of our buddies is dueling,\Nwe support him all the way.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.07,0:11:33.72,Default,,0,0,0,,So think positive, or\Nyou're going overboard.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.15,0:11:35.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi, Yugi, he's our man.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.17,0:11:37.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.49,0:11:41.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I know Yugi's gonna get through\Nthis just like you always do.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.23,0:11:46.45,Default,,0,0,0,,All the ghosts and evil spirits in\Nthis duel are freaking me out, Seto.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.53,0:11:47.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Nonsense.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.51,0:11:48.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Spirits don't exist.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.01,0:11:52.65,Default,,0,0,0,,The only thing Yugi has to be afraid\Nof is losing this duel and his
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.73,0:11:56.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Egyptian god card when all five\Nletters appear on the destiny board.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.91,0:12:00.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Not that it matters, since\NI'll win everything in the end.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.47,0:12:05.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid this duel is\Nalmost over. Too bad,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.43,0:12:09.90,Default,,0,0,0,,there's no hope left One more attack\Nto your life points and you're finished
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.05,0:12:15.37,Default,,0,0,0,,He's right. If I attack him with one\Nmore monster that's possessed I'll
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.45,0:12:18.91,Default,,0,0,0,,lose the rest of my life points and\Nbe eliminated from the finals If
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.99,0:12:23.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I could only figure out how to destroy\Nthe evil ghost of Dark Sanctuary
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.21,0:12:28.31,Default,,0,0,0,,There must be a way But how can I\Ndestroy something I can't even see?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.39,0:12:29.99,Default,,0,0,0,,What's the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.33,0:12:32.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps you would like\Nto forfeit the duel?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.89,0:12:33.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll never quit.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.23,0:12:35.53,Default,,0,0,0,,This duel isn't over,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.63,0:12:39.79,Default,,0,0,0,,and I know I have something in my\Nhand that can help turn things around.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.87,0:12:40.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.95,0:12:42.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe those cards can help.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.81,0:12:44.83,Default,,0,0,0,,I place two cards face down.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.87,0:12:47.45,Default,,0,0,0,,And end my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.55,0:12:51.87,Default,,0,0,0,,So, I see that you haven't yet\Nrealized that nothing can save you now.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.17,0:12:54.83,Default,,0,0,0,,It's merely a matter of time, Yugi. Wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.39,0:12:59.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I can assure you that your evil ghost of\NDark Sanctuary is in for a rude awakening.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.99,0:13:02.69,Default,,0,0,0,,And once it's gone, I'll\Nbe free to attack you.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.77,0:13:05.54,Default,,0,0,0,,You're no match for the\Npower of my deck, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.63,0:13:06.95,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll see about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.35,0:13:08.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Time is running out.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.11,0:13:10.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at the destiny board.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.75,0:13:11.83,Default,,0,0,0,,The third letter.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.29,0:13:13.21,Default,,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.83,0:13:14.66,Default,,0,0,0,,N.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.87,0:13:17.99,Default,,0,0,0,,F-I-N.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.15,0:13:20.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Two short turns and it's all over.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.71,0:13:27.07,Default,,0,0,0,,The Destiny Board is displaying three\Nletters. I'm aware of that. That'll
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.15,0:13:32.79,Default,,0,0,0,,do I play Souls of the Forgotten And\Nsacrifice it to keep Dark Sanctuary
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.53,0:13:40.03,Default,,0,0,0,,It's time for you to try and attack\Nme again if you dare, but remember,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.25,0:13:46.15,Default,,0,0,0,,One of your monsters is possessed. So\Nbe careful. Now make your move. I'll do
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.23,0:13:51.45,Default,,0,0,0,,it with pleasure I have a plan to\Ndemolish your evil ghost once and for all.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.57,0:13:53.41,Default,,0,0,0,,It can't be. It is.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.55,0:13:55.07,Default,,0,0,0,,And once your ghost is gone,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.15,0:13:58.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I won't have to worry about\Nmy monsters being possessed.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.45,0:14:01.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I have a feeling Yugi's about\Nto turn this thing around.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.51,0:14:04.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi, give this horror\Nshow a happy ending.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.21,0:14:09.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi will certainly need something\Npowerful to get himself out of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.41,0:14:11.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's see what he has planned.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.13,0:14:13.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Say goodbye to your ghost.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.41,0:14:16.21,Default,,0,0,0,,My invisible ghost is\Npossessing a monster now.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.71,0:14:20.67,Default,,0,0,0,,So, why don't you figure out\Nwhere it is and then destroy it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.97,0:14:23.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't have to figure out\Nwhere your dark ghost is.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.93,0:14:27.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I have a card in my deck\Nthat can find it for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.33,0:14:29.21,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, behold!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.99,0:14:32.21,Default,,0,0,0,,The trap card collected power!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.61,0:14:36.41,Default,,0,0,0,,It forces certain magic cards\Nto focus their effect on Karibo.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.93,0:14:46.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Why would Yugi use collective\Npower on a weak card like Karibo?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.99,0:14:49.73,Default,,0,0,0,,All it does is allow\Nhis pathetic monster to
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.81,0:14:52.75,Default,,0,0,0,,absorb the effects of a\Nfew magic cards That won't
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.83,0:14:56.05,Default,,0,0,0,,save him from Bacora's\NDark Sanctuary Unless it
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.13,0:14:59.65,Default,,0,0,0,,also absorbed the ghost\NSo who's in control now?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.99,0:15:03.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I knew that your evil ghost\Nlived within Dark Sanctuary
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.03,0:15:04.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Therefore,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.94,0:15:08.90,Default,,0,0,0,,I knew I had to play my trap card\NCollective Powers Because it would
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.99,0:15:12.93,Default,,0,0,0,,force your evil ghost right out of\Nits hiding place and into Coribo
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.59,0:15:22.33,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you plan to do? Simple,\NI'll use this a Magic Card called
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.41,0:15:27.95,Default,,0,0,0,,exile of the wicked which will\Nautomatically destroy my koribo so
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.03,0:15:29.85,Default,,0,0,0,,exile of the wicked wipe out my
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.93,0:15:30.97,Default,,0,0,0,,koribo and his
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.05,0:15:37.31,Default,,0,0,0,,dark ghost and now
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.39,0:15:43.43,Default,,0,0,0,,evil spirit of dark sanctuary be\Ngone You may have defeated my ghost,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.63,0:15:45.89,Default,,0,0,0,,but my destiny board\Nwill still destroy you in
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.97,0:15:48.62,Default,,0,0,0,,only two turns when it\Ncompletes its message.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.91,0:15:49.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't count on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.23,0:15:52.82,Default,,0,0,0,,This duel isn't over\Nand it's still my move.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.59,0:15:54.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Hooray!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.50,0:15:55.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Way to go, Yugi!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.25,0:15:58.63,Default,,0,0,0,,It's time for a little chat.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.05,0:16:04.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Just in case you haven't noticed,\Nyou've lost control of this duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.51,0:16:05.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Just what do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.35,0:16:10.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Your opponent has crushed your\Nstrategy by vanquishing your ghost.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.21,0:16:12.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Go away.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.12,0:16:13.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't need help.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.71,0:16:14.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't be a fool.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.11,0:16:16.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I said go!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.35,0:16:18.35,Default,,0,0,0,,You seem to forget that\Nwe have an agreement,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.43,0:16:22.91,Default,,0,0,0,,so if you're still interested in those\NMillennium Items, you'll listen to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.99,0:16:27.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Remember, you fool, if you lose this\Nduel, you'll be removed from the finals,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.39,0:16:30.80,Default,,0,0,0,,making you incapable of winning\Nme the Egyptian God Cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.07,0:16:32.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I won't lose, Merit.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.87,0:16:34.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid that's hard for me to believe
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.83,0:16:37.42,Default,,0,0,0,,based on the way you've\Nbeen dueling so far.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.77,0:16:38.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Then watch me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.01,0:16:41.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Win this or no deal
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.31,0:16:43.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Alright,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.37,0:16:46.91,Default,,0,0,0,,now it's time to bring back a\Nmonster from the graveyard I play
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.99,0:16:51.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Monster Reborn. I'll bring back\Na monster from your graveyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.59,0:16:55.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Dark Necrofear returned.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.17,0:17:01.79,Default,,0,0,0,,So say goodbye to your Dark\NSanctuary Since destroying Dark
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.87,0:17:06.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Necrofear released it. I knew bringing\Nit back would defeat it. No, And
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.79,0:17:10.35,Default,,0,0,0,,now that Dark Sanctuary is gone\NI'm afraid that you are no longer
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.43,0:17:14.27,Default,,0,0,0,,permitted to have more than five\Nmagic cards in play at one time.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.45,0:17:16.55,Default,,0,0,0,,This may foil some of your plans.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.51,0:17:22.71,Default,,0,0,0,,And now I'll attack your life\Npoints directly with Dark Necrofear!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.37,0:17:28.27,Default,,0,0,0,,All right,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.57,0:17:33.16,Default,,0,0,0,,this duel's almost done, since you've\Nlost more than half of your life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.23,0:17:37.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I add the fourth letter\Nto the destiny board.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.39,0:17:40.43,Default,,0,0,0,,letter A.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.51,0:17:42.67,Default,,0,0,0,,F-I-N-A.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.91,0:17:44.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Your word is final.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.91,0:17:47.68,Default,,0,0,0,,It's too bad you'll never\Nplay the last letter.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.81,0:17:49.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at your dual disc.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.23,0:17:53.75,Default,,0,0,0,,You have five magic cards in play\Nand you have no room for any others.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.01,0:17:57.09,Default,,0,0,0,,So if you want to play the\Nlast letter of your message,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.17,0:18:01.81,Default,,0,0,0,,you must discard your dark door magic\Ncard and its effect on my monsters,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.29,0:18:05.06,Default,,0,0,0,,allowing me to attack\Nmore than once in a turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.25,0:18:08.05,Default,,0,0,0,,And with no monsters to\Nprotect you and only twelve
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.13,0:18:10.87,Default,,0,0,0,,hundred life points my\Nthree monsters would wipe
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.95,0:18:15.19,Default,,0,0,0,,you out in one turn the\Ndecision is yours this
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.27,0:18:18.89,Default,,0,0,0,,can't be true stick a fork\Nin that guy because he's
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.97,0:18:23.99,Default,,0,0,0,,done be glad though what\Nseto it's not over i think
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.07,0:18:26.93,Default,,0,0,0,,bakora has something else\Nplanned for yugi what's
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.01,0:18:31.35,Default,,0,0,0,,that fool doing need i point\Nout that you're trapped
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.43,0:18:36.09,Default,,0,0,0,,i know so shall i control\Nyour mind and take over
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.65,0:18:37.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Never!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.56,0:18:41.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I plan to overpower this pathetic\Nduelist on my own, Merrick!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.29,0:18:44.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Now prepare yourself, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.49,0:18:47.25,Default,,0,0,0,,It's my move, and this\Nduel is far from over.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.35,0:18:53.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I've done it, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.75,0:18:56.63,Default,,0,0,0,,The time has arrived for\Nme to regain my control.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.41,0:19:00.41,Default,,0,0,0,,With this card! Oh, no! Hold on.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.57,0:19:03.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi just had this guy in\Nthe palm of his hand, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.15,0:19:05.67,Default,,0,0,0,,It seems like he just drew\Na pretty powerful card.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.75,0:19:07.01,Default,,0,0,0,,This can't be good.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.81,0:19:10.13,Default,,0,0,0,,It's all over, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.53,0:19:13.79,Default,,0,0,0,,The card I hold in my hand is\Nmy key to annihilating you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.87,0:19:15.34,Default,,0,0,0,,What card have you drawn?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.99,0:19:18.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Something that will help\Nme take all that you have.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.87,0:19:21.59,Default,,0,0,0,,The fate of the world\Ndepends on my victory.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.57,0:19:54.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Yu-Gi-Oh!
